On Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:05:21 -0700, Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com> wrote:
>> mbsync is an IMAP client of both Dovecot and Fastmail. Its channel
>> names only lists and Archive (Patterns lists Archive in mbsyncrc), so
>> anything in INBOX stays on lab-mail.
>
> No reason to just do lists and Archive. It should sync the entire mail
> account.

Agreed. It now syncs the whole account, in "[PATCH v6 00/10]
jails/instances/lab-mail: Build the list's mail hub" [1]. Patches 1-9
are v5 unchanged, and the new patch 10, "[PATCH v6 10/10]
jails/instances/lab-mail: Sync the whole Fastmail account" [2], does
the work:

- mbsync syncs every folder (Patterns *), and creates on lab-mail a
  folder that is new on Fastmail (Create Near). Expunge and Remove
  stay None.
- Dovecot's INBOX moves into the maildir, at
  /data/mail/maildir/INBOX, so it is synced like any other folder.
- The ACL keeps readers to the list. The account holds more than the
  list, and any login may read, so readers may list and read only
  lists and Archive. Pat and mbsync keep their rights everywhere.
  mbsync also gets the create right.

One risk to check first. Outside lists and Archive, the ACL names no
owner or anyone, and every login is the mailbox owner. If Dovecot then
gives the owner its default of every right, which I could not test
without Dovecot here, any reader could read and change the whole
account. Acceptance step 7 now checks that a reader cannot SELECT
INBOX and sees only lists and Archive. Please run it before the jail
takes readers.

Also, any post that landed in /data/mail/dovecot/inbox before Sieve
was in place is left behind when INBOX moves. Move it into lists from
an IMAP client as pat@p7x.dev before applying patch 10. The cover
letter has the details.

